Package: cohortflow
Title: Define and Apply Cohort Inclusion/Exclusion Criteria
Version: 0.0.0.9009
Authors@R:
    person("Matthew", "Moore", , "matthew.moore@auckland.ac.nz", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0730-8027"))
Description: Define inclusion and exclusion criteria for cohort studies using
    formulas or functions, apply them to data, and render the resulting
    attrition flow as CONSORT flow diagrams, tables, or narrative text.
    Supports hierarchical designs (participants nested in clusters/sites) and
    flexible grouping for reporting. Criteria pipelines can be serialised to
    YAML for reproducibility and sharing.
    Parts of this package were developed with the assistance of GitHub Copilot
    (powered by Claude), an AI coding assistant.
